<title>FRANCE: Chargeurs confirms 1998 profit aim.</title>
<headline>Chargeurs confirms 1998 profit aim.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chargeurs International on Wednesday confirmed its 1998 profit aim of three percent of sales.</p>
<p>Managing director Eduardo Malone told the annual general meeting: &quot;We fixed ourselves an objective to hit three percent of sales in three years, I confirm this objective and if the sales are favourable we could even do better,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The profit objective was set in 1996 when Chargeurs was split up in Pathe and Chargeurs International.</p>
<p>The 1996 profit was 136 million francs on sales of 8.67 billion against a pro-forma 1995 loss of 65 million francs.</p>
</text>
